                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.0. Add catalase and MgSO4 to 10 ml of distilled water each, and sterilize separately by filtration. Cool down autoclaved main solution to 50\u00b0C, and aseptically add catalase and MgSO4 solution."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 5.6. Sterilize at 121\u00b0C for 15 min."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Dissolve ingredients (except cysteine and sulfide), adjust pH to 7.0, bring medium to the boil, then cool to room temperature under 100% N2 gas. Dispense under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. After sterilization add cysteine and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas."
                    }
